92186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132361 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132361 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186551898 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186132361 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "69e5f672-7f5d-5b04-9df7-06332705d41d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133617 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5614" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133617 #edb/ref 1071 "| $x_1$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** | **$5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x_2$ | **$7$** | **$6.5$** | **$6$** | **$5$** | **$3$** |\n| $y$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ | $9$ | $15$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the plane $y=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x_1 + \\beta_2 x_2$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as \n\n![](images/9d/9da2a49a4bab645fa1b8ea3f98e6aa6135b191e121d0cc78a73b517fbc510fc0.png)\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. Find  $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ in this context." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133617 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18e10da5-f3e1-52d2-b2c6-2a69a1bf1947" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133617 #edb/ref 1074 "| $x_1$ | **$\\color{blue}1$** | **$\\color{blue}2$** | **$\\color{blue}3$** | **$\\color{blue}4$** | **$\\color{blue}5$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x_2$ | **$\\color{purple}7$** | **$\\color{purple}6.5$** | **$\\color{purple}6$** | **$\\color{purple}5$** | **$\\color{purple}3$** |\n| $y$ | $\\color{red}1$ | $\\color{red}2$ | $\\color{red}5$ | $\\color{red}9$ | $\\color{red}15$ |\n\nThe coefficients of the plane \n\n$$\ny=\\beta_0 + \\beta_1 x_1 + \\beta_2 x_2\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}}$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 6.5 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{0} \\\\ {\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 15\\end{bmatrix}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector.\n\nThus, we have\n![](images/b5/b5302251a49a45514a55d2987289548e2a55917884ff4c240be081ba512a970e.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186133618 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5615" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133618 #edb/ref 1071 "| $x_1$ | **$1$** | **$2$** | **$3$** | **$4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x_2$ | **$-8$** | **$-2$** | **$6$** | **$15$** |\n| $x_3$ | **$8$** | **$6$** | **$4$** | **$2$** |\n| $y$ | $10$ | $20$ | $40$ | $60$ |\n\nThe vector of coefficients of the hyperplane $y = \\beta_1 x_1 + \\beta_2 x_2 +\\beta_3 x_3$ that best fits the data above can be found using multiple linear regression as \n\n![](images/3f/3f86f03e3a32ede2ac18d6c39f62de5686a74d4050b8c1d7aa2a6fc3e2cdddbb.png)\n\nwhere $X$ is the corresponding design matrix and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector. Find  $X$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ in this context." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133618 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ab93579a-f7a1-5cfe-85ce-5a4d5722e7b7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133618 #edb/ref 1074 "| $x_1$ | **$\\color{blue}1$** | **$\\color{blue}2$** | **$\\color{blue}3$** | **$\\color{blue}4$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x_2$ | **$\\color{purple}-8$** | **$\\color{purple}-2$** | **$\\color{purple}6$** | **$\\color{purple}15$** |\n| $x_3$ | **$\\color{green}8$** | **$\\color{green}6$** | **$\\color{green}4$** | **$\\color{green}2$** |\n| $y$ | $\\color{red}10$ | $\\color{red}20$ | $\\color{red}40$ | $\\color{red}60$ |\n\n \n\nThe coefficients of the hyperplane  \n\n$$\ny= \\beta_1 x_1 + \\beta_2 x_2 +\\beta_3 x_3\n$$\n\nthat best fits the data can be found as the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\boldsymbol{\\beta}}}$ to the system \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{X}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -8 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 3 & 6 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 15 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{\\beta }{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{\\beta }_{1} \\\\ {\\beta }_{2} \\\\ {\\beta }_{3}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{y}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ 20 \\\\ 40 \\\\ 60\\end{bmatrix}}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $X$ is the design matrix, $\\boldsymbol{\\beta}$ is the parameter vector, and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the observation vector.\n\nThus, we have \n\n![](images/c8/c83d300d9e6e1c1bd61fc49c4e849ab373d902beb3cd12ef501461a86bd1a08c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050830 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134388 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186271968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278252 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186278253 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373764 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186373883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400839 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186401130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186402789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186552410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186552418 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1039 "Identifying Elements of a Multiple Linear Regression" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186133617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133808 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "75e33c97-0499-5829-9886-be30b00989ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186133809 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186134114 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [